==Overview==
<tabber>
Pros=
{{Overview|Pros
|'''General'''
* Extremely high combo potential.
* Compatible with air PvP.
* High damage.
* Both moves have no endlag.
* Has very short cooldowns, fast [M1] attack speed, and no dash on the fourth [M1] attack, making it a good choice for grinding.
* Drains [[Instinct]] dodges efficiently.
* All moves can damage [[Sea Beast]]s.
* Both moves can [[Instinct/Break|break instinct]].
* Both moves work with Awakened [[Buddha]].

|'''[Z] Scorching Azure'''
* Good range.
* Amazing stun.

|'''[X] Infernal Firestorm'''
* Decent mobility.
* Can hit multiple targets.
* Good [[AoE]].
* Decent stun.
}}

|-|Cons=
{{Overview|Cons
|'''General'''
* Cannot hit [[Blade]] users.
* Requires good aiming ability and quick reaction.
* Difficult to obtain.
* High mastery requirements.
* Both moves can be [[Instinct]] tricked.
|'''[Z] Scorching Azure'''
* The knockback trajectory can make combos more difficult, such as having to aim [[Godhuman]]'s {{Ability|Godhuman|Z}} at the enemy.
* Single target.
* Can be dodged if not aimed correctly.
* Requires precise aim.
* Does not true-stun, meaning the target can still move and use abilities if they Instinct-trick this attack.

|'''[X] Infernal Firestorm'''
* Mediocre range.
* After holding and rushing to the target, a small delay makes it possible for enemies to use [[Flash Step]].
* Enemies can punish the player if they hold the skill for too long.
* The blue flame doesn't true-stun in either the hold or tap versions, meaning the target can counterattack during the ability's duration if they use Instinct Trick.}}
</tabber>

==Trivia==
* The Fox Lamp is more recommended for grinding by pairing it with [[Buddha]].
* The Fox Lamp's {{Ability|Z}} cannot be held for more than 15 seconds
* The Fox Lamp does not turn black when [[Aura]] is active, though [[Skins|Aura colors]] still appear (Similar to the [[Shark Anchor]]).
* Despite being a [[Swords|sword]], the Fox Lamp resembles a lantern rather than a blade.
* The [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Katakana Japanese symbols] (キツネ) shown when charging {{Ability|Z}} and {{Ability|X}} (The player can briefly see the symbols as it is spun at a very fast speed), mean "Kitsune" which when translated means "Fox" in English 
** "Kitsune" can also be written as the kanji character "狐"
** Or "Kitsune" can also be written as the hiragana symbols "きつね"
* {{Ability|X}}, when tapped, bears a slight resemblance to [[Dragon Talon]]'s {{Ability|Dragon Talon|Z}}.
* When paired with awakened buddha it gives little stun making it easier to kill the players but if you repeat using m1 the player you will get a suspicious kill
** Fox Lamp's [M1] attacks' sound effect is similar to [[Dragon Breath]] and [[Dragon Talon]], but with a slightly lower pitch and a slight reverb.
*The fox lamp's {{Ability|X}} can clip through soft floors. For example, [[Tiki Outpost]], [[Café|Cafe]], etc can be clipped through.

